    <!-- FAQ -->
    <string name="faq_screen_title">Frequently asked questions</string>
    <string-array name="faq_questions">
        <item>What is Solocards?</item>
        <item>What is flashcard?</item>
        <item>How to use flashcards for study?</item>
        <item>What is a quiz?</item>
        <item>What every game mode means?</item>
        <item>What is a scripting feature?</item>
        <item>What I can do in cloud storage?</item>
        <item>What\'s profile information the cloud storage take?</item>
        <item>What if I see «Can\'t open file» when I import quiz/progress?</item>
        <item>Where the contact information?</item>
        <item>What is option blank?</item>
        <item>Why Solocards?</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="faq_answers">
        <item>Solocards is an offline-first lightweight flashcard app</item>
        <item>Flashcard is simply just a card with a question and answer on different sides</item>
        <item>Here is the most common way how to use them: Take any card and make it facing the question side. Your goal is to think of the answer in your head. Then flip the card and verify yourself</item>
        <item>It\'s a list of flashcards (basically the deck)</item>
        <item>In the editor click play and then help button. You will see the description of every mode</item>
        <item>You can find tutorial in a code editor</item>
        <item>Cloud storage is an optional feature that stores your quizzes in the cloud. It makes easier to transfer and synchronize the progress between devices</item>
        <item>Only email</item>
        <item>Make sure you pick the quiz file, not a progress file (or vice versa). If it doesn\'t fix anything, contact me via email</item>
        <item>In the About menu</item>
        <item>It\'s the list of all incorrect options of the card</item>
        <item>Solocards is the lightweight card manager which is the best for every kind of science, especially for math and computer science. The scripting feature makes card-making experience smooth</item>
    </string-array>

